          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On December 8, 2009, between 7:20 and 7:30 AM, a witness observed for 10 to 20 seconds in the sky a glowing ball. Its movement was horizontal on a west-east trajectory. The ball disintegrated by fragmenting into two or three pieces before disappearing. The described phenomenon, moving horizontally at a high speed and splitting (\"exploding\") into several pieces, appears to correspond to the characteristics of an atmospheric reentry.",
